      "name": "industry_vertical",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A meaningful categorical axis derived from the description; strong feature for predicting regional cluster (e.g. VC on Sand Hill Road). Samples are well-grounded readings of the text. 23andme labeled consumer_internet is defensible though healthcare/genomics would be arguably better, minor imprecision."
    },
    {
      "name": "tech_stack_focus",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Captures a distinct technology axis not redundant with industry_vertical; useful for clustering. 'not_present' used honestly for silent rows (VC firms, consulting), which is correct behavior. Values track the source text well."
    },
    {
      "name": "stage_signals",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
      "source_groundedness": 0.55,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "Company stage could help distinguish clusters, but the values are weakly supported. Descriptions rarely state stage; 'growth_stage' for 280 Group and 'established_public' for 23andme are confident assertions the text does not support (23andme description says nothing about being public). Heavy inference beyond the source. 'venture_capital' as a stage also just restates industry."
    },
    {
      "name": "market_reach",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.7,
      "source_groundedness": 0.6,
      "hallucination_observed": true,
      "rationale": "B2B/B2C/global axis is a plausible clustering feature, but overlaps somewhat with service_model. Groundedness is moderate: labeling VC firms 'b2b_focused' is a stretch and 'global_enterprise' vs 'b2b_focused' distinctions are often not stated in the short descriptions, inviting invented specificity."
    },
    {
      "name": "service_model",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Distinct and useful axis (SaaS vs hardware vs consulting vs VC). Sample values are sound readings: 280 Group->consulting_staffing, 5AM->venture_investing, Addepar->saas_cloud_platform. Some 'saas_cloud_platform' assignments (23andme) are inferred but reasonable."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
  "source_groundedness": 0.75,
  "rationale": "The added columns provide several genuinely distinct categorical axes (industry, tech, service model, market reach) that give real leverage for predicting a regional cluster from business descriptions, with limited redundancy. Groundedness is generally good, with honest 'not_present' handling. The main weakness is stage_signals and parts of market_reach, which assert stage/reach specifics (public status, growth stage, global) that the short descriptions frequently do not state, indicating over-confident inference on silent rows."
}
